    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d369">

                <pb facs="0383" n="371" sameAs="frus:frus1939v01/pg371"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">760C.62/1022: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Kennedy</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-08-26T12:00:00+01:00">August 26,
                            1939—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received August 26—6:25 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1263. Omitted from my number 1262, August 25, midnight, was the important item
                    that Henderson’s message stated Hitler said the only one to benefit from a war
                    between Germany and England would be Japan who might very well become the
                    dominating factor in the world.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kennedy</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
